Z||000003||FieroLisa||12-12-2000||05:12 PM||||firstfiero: I absolutely can't stand it when people say "Fiero? Ain't those the ones that caught fire?" No d@mnit if they all caught fire then how come mine's still driving un-charred???? Where's the smoke and flames? UGGGG. OK I'm done now. No wait I'm not, someone said to me yesterday, "You actually try to race that piece of $hit?" I was gettin mad...<P><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>*Updated Website* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A> ||||reg||8
Z||000004||Fformula88||12-12-2000||05:18 PM||||I have had people ask me if it will burn up EVERYWHERE!  Even another customer at an oil change place!  Oh, and he had one I didn't hear as much, he also asked if the suspension was always out of alignment (???). It was a new one on me, but I said no since I have had it aligned once and have had no problems since!<P>I find that I get a good deal of respect in the Fiero.  There are the punk ricer kids who just are stupid... but I am rarely challenged by other cars on the road.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||12-12-2000||06:02 PM||||I try to beat 'em to the punch. I'll make a  remark about Fiero Flambe', or some such. <BR>And, as you said, if you're standing there, next to your Fiero, it's very obvious that it didn't burn to the ground. Once I have their attention, I then explain about the "bad rod" situation with the 84s, and the recall. Bottom line is, all the ones that were going to burn down probably already have. The rest have been fixed. <BR>They usually give me a stupid look and say "oh".||||reg||1
Z||000006||86SE||12-12-2000||06:17 PM||||When ever someone dises the Fiero, like they say "There just little plastic death traps", or "Fieros are junk" or something like that, I don't say a single work, just laugh quietly and tell them to bring what ever car they drive for a little race.  90% of the time after I show em up, they shut their mouth about the Fiero, they will just joke but they know the truth that the Fiero is a tough race to win. Its just funny how their attitude changes in 15 seconds.||||reg||12
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||12-12-2000||06:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>I didn't mean that their not cool looking cars....it's just thier over achieving four cyl. aren't much of a match for the fiero v6. They just act stunned when you drill them.   </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've never had the pleasure of racing a Prelude.. but I imagine a V6 Prelude would be a pretty fair match, and would smoke the Fiero in the top end. From what I hear, their handling is pretty good too.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||KnightRyder31||12-12-2000||06:40 PM||||I don't care for Fiero-haters!!! <BR>I hate them!!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||afRaceR||12-12-2000||06:51 PM||||This is probably one of my oddest and funniest fiero stories. One day I was at work and I was having a heated discussion with this *******  about how he thought all Fiero's will catch fire and I was really getting pissed. <P>Well, two hours after the conversation someone runs in and yells there's a car on fire. The guy gave my a quick grin and I just flipped him off. Turns out a Ford F150 completely burned to the ground. People always forget how the recall plaqued Ford had a little ignition switch recall on about half the models they produced because the switches would cause the car to catch on fire.<P>After the fire department put out the fire, I went and parked my car beside the truck and laughed my ass off. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||firstfiero||12-13-2000||10:14 AM||||They never made a prelude with a v6...only 4 cylinders. I raced a kid 2 fridays ago with a brand new one. His friend in the passanger seat was hollering out the window to me asking if I wanted to race my P.O.S. I decided not to hammer it right away he had that little rice burner screaming and I hadn't left 2nd gear yet. half way down the block I hamered it...fished tailed a bit but by that time i had a car lengths lead on him. when we came to the next red light he stayed far behind so he didn't have to look me in the eye.   Their good handeling cars but in a straight shoot out they don't our v6.||||reg||6
Z||000011||count_iblis||12-13-2000||11:01 AM||||ALthough Im not a ricer, I think you all should give a little more respect to them.  Actually from what ive seen around here and in Ohio, more ricers give respect to the fiero then most redneck muscle car owners do. Oh for you who will flame me on the "redneck" saying its just the same as you calling the people out there ricers.  Plus Im surronded by them here so I should know.  <P>Later ||||reg||8
Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||12-13-2000||11:04 AM||||I saw a 2001 Prelude on display at a mall in the summer, and I was practically drooling over it.. I was sure the sticker said it was a V6.. oh well.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
