Z||000019||DaRkLoRD||12-13-2000||04:48 PM||||I like the new Preludes, and the looks of the Acura Integra.. I've never driven or even sat in either, so I can't really comment on how they handle, feel, etc.<P>I think civics are inexpensive, efficient cars.. but they're not sports cars.. and definitely not in the same class as turbo MR2s...<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Fformula88||12-13-2000||08:12 PM||||Overall I think the Prelude's are nice cars.  I just wish they would figure out how to make the headlights look more "normal".  They get great reviews for handling, and have a lot of horsepower for a 4 cylinder.  Civics aren't fast, but its amazing how many aftermarket parts are available for them!  They can be made to go very fast, although for the investment cost you could buy a car that was fast from the factory.  But I give a lot of credit to those owners who actually do all those mods (not the ricers who just plaster stickers all over their stock Civics).  ||||reg||1
Z||000021||88formula||12-13-2000||10:36 PM||||I saw a Honda Civic run a 13.3 at the track this summer when a new 2000 Corvette ran a 13.6 right after. The civic spun the ****  out of his tires off the line too. I have a new respect for four cylinder imports now. I never though a four cylinder car could out run a 2000 Corvette with front wheel drive. <P>I raced a late model Honda prelude with my formula and he had me by a 3/4-car length by 60 mph and after that I could not keep up with him.<P>I raced a Porsche 944 and he left me in the dust. <P>I raced a 91 Ford mustang and he left me in the dust.<P>I raced a 99 Camaro and although I could not beat him I took him in a corner real good.<P>I raced a Honda CRX and believe it or not he killed me (was modified for sure).<P>I raced a 327 cu. in. 67 Corvette and beat him by half a car (his engine was running on 7 cylinders).<P>I raced a 99 Bonneville and he beat me by a half a car.<P>I raced a new VW jetta (four) and beat him by about two cars. <P>Is the stock v6 fiero fast, not really by today’s standards? The 88formula only goes 0-60 in 8 seconds and the quarter mile in 16 seconds with the five speed, which is what I have. My Fathers new econo-car Toyota Corolla gets to 60 mph in 8.3 seconds and does the quarter mile in 16.6 seconds and my two-ton Toyota Tundra in 7.9 seconds. The fiero is not some super car that is untouchably fast in stock form. It is only a little above average for acceleration. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||Tina||12-13-2000||11:35 PM||||Well that explains a lot, with the headlights I mean.<BR>Hello,too.<BR>See where I come from was entirely different meaning.<BR>Flashing Headlights from behind you= Move over ,your're in my way.<BR>Headlights aproching you: Radar or cop ahead.<P>Tina<BR>Transplanted Autobahn Driver<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000023||PearlBlueSoul||12-14-2000||10:20 AM||||Wazaaap..hehe..been away for a while but it's cool to see the board doing well<P>Darklord, thanks for the compliment!  Belive me, I have to say the same thing about ricers.  Said it before, and I'll say it again:  9 times out of 10 you can smoke what you're racing when it comes to a riced out car.  I speak from lots of personal experience.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  hehe<P><P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
